<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Patio engineering in Perth usually starts with one question from the kit supplier, the builder or the council: where are the structural details? A roofed patio, carport or shed that needs a building permit needs drawings and, in most cases, a structural engineer's certificate showing it will handle the wind and sit properly on the ground. Kings Park Structural Co is advertising for an independent structural engineering firm. You call, we pass the job on, and the engineer quotes and contracts with you directly.</p><p>Plenty of small structures don't need a permit at all, and it's worth knowing that before you pay anyone. Read the exemptions below first. If yours falls outside them, the engineer who quotes your job will want the size, where it sits on the block, what it's made of and whether it's fixed to the house. The fee side is covered on <a href="/structural-engineer-cost-perth/">what a structural engineer costs in Perth</a>.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Permit check first</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The Building Regulations 2012 exempt some small sheds, roofless pergolas and low retaining walls from a permit. Checking whether yours is one of them is the cheapest step in the whole job.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Site-specific drawings</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Drawings for your block and your structure rather than a standard detail off a list, with slab and footing design based on the soil.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Wind loading to AS/NZS 1170.2</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A patio or carport roof catches wind like a sail, and uplift is what the design has to hold down. The certificate states the design gust wind speed used, under AS/NZS 1170.2 or AS 4055.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Footings matched to the site class</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The certificate states the site class under AS 2870. Most Perth metro ground is sand, normally Class A, but loose sand is Class P and clay sites turn up particularly in the Perth Hills.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">A certificate the surveyor can rely on</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The Building Act calls it a technical certificate. It lists the drawings it covers, and a certified permit application includes each one the building surveyor relied on.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Already built without a permit</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Unauthorised work is regularised with a building approval certificate, form BA13. One Perth firm's outline of that route includes an engineer's inspection and certification of what's there.</p>
      </div>
</div>
